<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of second round, second leg matches in African club soccer competitions on Saturday:</p>
<p>Confederation of African Football (CAF) Cup</p>
<p>In Kampala: Kampala City Council (Uganda) 1 AS Bantous (Zaire) 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Mohamed Dyansi 43</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Kampala City Council win 1-0 on aggregate. The first leg was cancelled because of the civil war in Zaire.</p>
<p>In Lagos: Jasper United (Nigeria) 2 Mohammedia (Morocco) 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Paul Kpoughol 30, Joe Okoh 79</p>
<p>Attendance: 16,000</p>
<p>Aggregate 2-2. Jasper United won 4-3 on penalties.</p>
</text>
